 "train_curve_note": "ep_rew_mean = SB3 rolling mean over the last 100 episodes of the terminal reward -3*W[task]*(score/norm[task][class]+penalty), W=(2/3,1/3), penalty = 0.3/deg of tilt peak above 60 deg (descend8 objective per case). Tasks are sampled with p=(2/3,1/3), so E[reward] = -(4/3*nod_obj + 1/3*dash_obj); objective_equiv = -ep_rew_mean*3/5 is exact only when nod_obj == dash_obj. Measured with the stochastic policy (Gaussian exploration noise, std 0.22 -> 0.08) on train cases cases8 offset 100000+gen*100 (gen = centre index 0..11, 660 episodes per centre); NOT the deterministic centre, so it is systematically worse than the reselect numbers."
